{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.C1SeriesConvergence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1SeriesConvergence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Normed"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.zeroCoeffAt_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.zeroCoeffAt_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":561,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L561-L567","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.zeroCoeffAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.zeroCoeffAt","kind":"def","line":555,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L555-L559","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.infCoeffAt_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.infCoeffAt_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":547,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L547-L553","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.infCoeffAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.infCoeffAt","kind":"def","line":541,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L541-L545","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.summable_infSideCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.summable_infSideCoeff","kind":"theorem","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L404-L506","doc":"**The `∞`-side series is entire.**\n\nThe recursion's two coefficients decay like `‖p‖^{-k}` and `‖p‖^{-2k}` while\nthe denominator tends to the nonzero constant `1 − p²`, so\n`summable_of_two_step_geometric` applies: the radius of convergence in `1/z`\nis infinite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.infSideCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.infSideCoeff","kind":"def","line":393,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L393-L399","doc":"`∞`-side coefficients: `h₀ = 1` and the two-term recursion of\n`computations/qbeta/c3_w2_c1_pole_divisor.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.infSideDen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.infSideDen","kind":"def","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L389-L391","doc":"Denominator of the `∞`-side recursion, `T²p³(1/p)^{2k} + (1−p²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.summable_of_two_step_geometric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.summable_of_two_step_geometric","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L270-L385","doc":"**A two-step recursion whose coefficients vanish geometrically is entire.**\n\nIf `‖a (k+2)‖ ≤ Dρᵏ · max ‖a (k+1)‖ ‖a k‖` for `k ≥ K`, with `0 < ρ < 1`, then\n`∑ aₖ uᵏ` converges for **every** `u` — the radius of convergence is `∞`.\n\nThe majorant is `M · ∏_{j<k} (c σʲ)` with `σ = √ρ`: the two-step lag costs\nexactly a square root, and `σ² = ρ` is what makes the induction close with a\nconstant `c` rather than a `k`-dependent one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.summable_zeroSideCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.summable_zeroSideCoeff","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L222-L266","doc":"**The `0`-side power series converges on the open unit disc.**\n\nThe radius of convergence of `∑ gₖ zᵏ` is at least `1`. The ratio\n`g_{k+2}/g_k = t²p^{2k}/(t²p^{2k} + (q−1)tp^k + (q−1))` tends to `1` like\n`1 + O(‖p‖^{-k})`, so the coefficients are bounded, which is all radius `≥ 1`\nneeds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.norm_zeroSideRatio_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.norm_zeroSideRatio_le","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L206-L220","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.norm_zeroSideTail_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.norm_zeroSideTail_le","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L179-L204","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.zeroSideRatio_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.zeroSideRatio_eq","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L169-L177","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.zeroSideCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.zeroSideCoeff","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L163-L167","doc":"`0`-side coefficients: `g₀ = 1`, `g₁ = 0`, `g_{k+2} = ratio(k+2)·g_k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.zeroSideTail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.zeroSideTail","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L159-L161","doc":"The relative size of the subleading part of the denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.zeroSideRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.zeroSideRatio","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L155-L157","doc":"The `0`-side recursion's ratio, `t²p^{2k} / (t²p^{2k} + (q−1)tp^k + (q−1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.summable_of_norm_coeff_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.summable_of_norm_coeff_le","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L141-L151","doc":"**Bounded coefficients ⇒ the power series converges on the open unit disc.**\n\ni.e. radius of convergence `≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.C1Series.norm_le_of_ratio_le_one_add_geometric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.C1Series.norm_le_of_ratio_le_one_add_geometric","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/C1SeriesConvergence.lean#L86-L139","doc":"**A two-step recursion whose ratio is `1 + O(geometric)` has bounded terms.**\n\nIf `‖a (k+2)‖ ≤ (1 + Cρᵏ)‖a k‖` for all `k ≥ K`, with `0 ≤ ρ < 1`, then `‖a‖`\nis bounded by an explicit constant: the telescoped product `∏(1 + Cρᵏ)` is\ncontrolled by `exp (C ∑ ρᵏ) ≤ exp (C/(1-ρ))`, and the finitely many terms below\nthe threshold are absorbed into the sum `∑_{j < K+2} ‖a j‖`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}